- op: discuss  # 72c1
  at: '2026-07-16T10:22:27Z'  # 72c1
  by: agent  # 72c1
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 72c1
  clock: 3  # 72c1
  nonce: 72c1  # 72c1
  message: "Fixed in PR #689 (dev b8e4d675a1). Cross-file 'new X(...)' now lands its 'instantiates' edge on the constructor node (Type.Type) instead of the class node; falls back to the class only when the type has no explicit ctor (implicit default). Behavioral evidence: live analyze_csharp probe — cross-file 'new WaveReader(\"a.wav\")' now targets dst.kind=constructor 'WaveReader.WaveReader' (was dst.kind=class 'WaveReader'), so a reverse-slice seeded on the ctor now reaches the construction call sites. Tests: test_csharp.py::TestCSharpSpecialCases::{test_cross_file_instantiation_targets_constructor, test_same_file_instantiation_targets_constructor, test_instantiation_without_explicit_ctor_targets_class}. Root cause: same-file resolution hit the ctor via symbol_by_name shadowing while cross-file resolver.lookup returned the class — now unified via the Type.Type key (C# CS0542 guarantees that key is a ctor). DOCUMENTED RESIDUAL: overloaded constructors collapse to the last-registered ctor in the global registry, so all instantiations of an overloaded type share one ctor anchor (arity-precise overload matching is a follow-up, filed separately)."  # 72c1
